## Installed skills

Record every skill installed into `.claude/skills/` during setup. Each
skill is **pinned to an exact commit SHA** (from the pinned-skills table in
the project-bootstrap reference for this project type) — never record a
bare branch. Before a skill counts as installed, its `SKILL.md` was read
and summarised in the Read-summary column (SKILL.md Step 4,
read-before-install). If no stack skills were installed (python/generic
default), delete the table rows below and write this sentence on its own
line instead: No stack skills installed for this project. (The
`--verify` content check looks for either a 40-character pinned SHA in
this file or that exact sentence on its own line.)

| Skill | Source URL | Pinned SHA | Date installed | Read-summary |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {{SKILL_NAME_1}} | {{SKILL_URL_1}} | {{SKILL_SHA_1}} | {{DATE}} | {{SKILL_READ_SUMMARY_1 — 2-3 lines: what instructions this skill loads into future sessions; flag any network access, credential use, or destructive commands it asks for}} |
| {{SKILL_NAME_2}} | {{SKILL_URL_2}} | {{SKILL_SHA_2}} | {{DATE}} | {{SKILL_READ_SUMMARY_2 — 2-3 lines, same requirements as above}} |

To bump a pin deliberately: clone the skill's repo, read the new
`SKILL.md` (and anything it loads), update the SHA + date + read-summary
here, and commit that change on its own — never bump silently as part of
feature work.

Workflow: the default checklist in CLAUDE.md (spec → plan → build →
separate review). If a different workflow framework was chosen at setup,
name it here instead — never run two at once.

